      "to": "Proper 18 (23)",
      "id": "a-second-rom-proper-5-10-a",
      "arc": "Paul's letter to the Romans, read straight through, is already a series — from the plight and gift of justification, through life in the Spirit and God's faithfulness to Israel, to the transformed common life.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "from": 1,
          "to": 4,
          "label": "Justified & freed (Rom 4–6)",
          "note": "Abraham's faith, peace with God, and the turn from death-in-sin to life-in-God."
        },
        {
          "from": 5,
          "to": 8,
          "label": "Life in the Spirit (Rom 7–8)",
          "note": "The war within, no condemnation, and nothing able to separate us from the love of God."
        },
        {
          "from": 9,
          "to": 11,
          "label": "God's faithfulness to Israel (Rom 9–11)",
          "note": "The hard mystery of election — and a mercy that finally reaches all."
        },
        {
          "from": 12,
          "to": 14,
          "label": "Living sacrifice (Rom 12–13)",
          "note": "Bodies offered as worship; love named as the fulfilling of the law."
        }
      ]
    },
